{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["עָקָר — it is all with qamatz, like from חָכָם one says אשה חֲכָמָה; from שָׁפָל — שְׁפָלָה — is not it likewise? From עָקָר one says עֲקָרָה. And so I have found in all the books of Sepharad."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The segment 'איננה כמו כן' is syntactically awkward; rendered hyper-literally. The point is that just as adjectives like חָכָם form feminine חֲכָמָה, so עָקָר forms עֲקָרָה, all with qamatz vocalization."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:38:28.066282843Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}